    "result_text": "The build passes green. \n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `contactPreference` rule: `EMAIL` when the owner has an email, otherwise `PHONE`.\n\nTwo small, low-impact changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `contactPreference` string field to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it (and it flows through the existing `GET /api/owners/{id}` response path unchanged).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping` annotation line to the existing `toOwnerDto` method with an inline expression:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"contactPreference\",\n       expression = \"java(owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank() ? \\\"EMAIL\\\" : \\\"PHONE\\\")\")\n   ```\n\nI kept structural impact minimal: no new methods or classes, no growth of any function body \u2014 just one annotation on an existing zero-body interface method plus a schema field. `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 both the `PHONE`-when-no-email and `EMAIL`-when-present cases pass, and the full suite is green.",
